{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1594776539/16/codegen_prompts/5.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/16`\n- 题号：`5`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1594776539/16/5.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"5\">\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内\"种子\"像素的颜色和数量，选择对应的纹理图案填充该区域，种子数量控制纹理的平铺相位。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 black，网格大小约 20x20。\n  - 网格中有若干由 grey 像素绘制的封闭边界，将网格划分为多个不规则的封闭区域（regions）。边界线宽为 1 像素，所有边界相互连通形成一张连通的\"墙壁\"网络。每个封闭区域的面积在 6-30 像素之间。\n  - 网格的底部两行是一个\"纹理图例\"区域，与上方的封闭区域用一条完整的 grey 水平线分隔。纹理图例中排列着 2-4 个并排的 3x3 彩色纹理方块，相邻方块之间用 1 列 grey 像素分隔。每个 3x3 纹理方块使用恰好两种颜色（一种为该纹理的\"主色\"，另一种为 black），形成独特的二值图案（如棋盘格、十字、对角线、边框等）。\n  - 上方的每个封闭区域内散布着 1-3 个彩色\"种子\"像素（seed pixels），种子像素的颜色与某个纹理方块的主色相同。一个区域内所有种子像素颜色相同。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步（纹理匹配）：每个封闭区域内种子像素的颜色决定了该区域应使用哪个纹理方块——颜色相同即为匹配。\n  - 第二步（纹理平铺）：将匹配的 3x3 纹理方块以周期平铺（tiling）的方式铺满整个网格平面（以网格左上角为对齐原点），然后仅保留落在该封闭区域内部的纹理像素。纹理中 black 位置保持 black，主色位置绘制为该纹理的主色。\n  - 第三步（种子数量调控相位）：如果区域内的种子像素数量为 2，则纹理平铺在水平方向偏移 1 像素；如果数量为 3，则在水平和竖直方向各偏移 1 像素；数量为 1 则不偏移。\n  - grey 边界像素在输出中保持不变。种子像素被纹理覆盖（不再可见）。纹理图例区域在输出中保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：种子颜色决定纹理选择，这是第一层推理；种子数量控制纹理平铺的相位偏移是第二层隐蔽规则——仅通过颜色匹配无法解释不同区域中相同纹理的像素位置差异，解题者必须注意种子数量与纹理偏移之间的对应关系。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：eval/dbff022c, eval/9385bd28, eval/581f7754, eval/8b7bacbf, train/98c475bf, train/20fb2937, train/aa62e3f4, train/6165ea8f\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3322\nmechanism=0.4094\nlexical=0.0119\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:sprite, object:template, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9385bd28\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3233\nmechanism=0.4274\nlexical=0.0134\ncode_feature=0.2500\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:counter, object:axis, object:marker, object:sprite, object:square, object:template, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:aligned, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:overlap, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9385bd28.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.\n- Scattered L-shaped corner markers of each marker color define opposite corners of axis-aligned rectangles.\n- Some markers are solid 2×2 blocks instead of corner pairs.\n\nRule:\n- Read legend bottom-to-top; for each entry find all pixels of that marker color.\n- Determine which two bbox corners carry L-shaped anchors — the *other* diagonal defines the fill region.\n- Fill the diamond (all shortest-path cells between those two corners) with the legend's fill color.\n- Solid 2×2 marker blocks are simply recolored to the fill color.\n- Later legend entries are protected from earlier fills.\n\nKey insight: The L-shaped anchors sit on the marker diagonal; the fill goes on the opposite diagonal of the bounding box.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color legend at bottom-left to find diagonal marker pairs of matching color, then fill the rectangle between them with the adjacent legend color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"diagonal pixel pair s with same color forming opposite corners of a rectangle (upper corner pixel)\",\n  \"dst\": \"diagonal pixel pair d with same color forming opposite corners of a rectangle (lower corner pixel)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.color == d.color && s and d are diagonally opposite\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill rectangle bounded by s and d with color from legend where legend.left == s.color gives fill_color = legend.right\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"legend is vertical stack of color pairs at bottom-left, each pair (left-right only) has marker color on left and fill color on right\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify legend as vertically stacked color pairs at bottom-left corner; Step 2: process legend entries from bottom to top; Step 3: for each legend entry (marker_color on left, fill_color on right), find all diagonal pairs of marker_color pixels; Step 4: fill rectangle between each diagonal pair with fill_color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-legend\",\n    \"diagonal-markers\",\n    \"rectangle-fill\",\n    \"ordered-processing\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"sometimes as 2x2 squares which count as two diagonal triangles; processing order matters for overlapping regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"581f7754\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3268\nmechanism=0.3760\nlexical=0.0128\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:axis, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:sprite, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/581f7754.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/581f7754.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide multi-color sprites to align their marker pixels with matching isolated border anchors.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Multi-color sprites in the interior; each has a minority-color \"marker\" pixel.\n- Isolated border pixels (non-bg with all 4-neighbors bg) act as anchors.\n\nRule:\n- Match each sprite to the border anchor sharing its marker color.\n- Top/bottom-edge anchor (non-corner): slide sprite horizontally so marker column = anchor column.\n- Left/right-edge anchor (or corner): slide sprite vertically so marker row = anchor row.\n\nKey insight: The anchor's edge position determines the slide axis — top/bottom means horizontal, left/right (or corner) means vertical.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"multi-color sprite s with a unique marker color (minority color inside s)\",\n  \"dst\": \"align to isolated border pixel d (same marker color)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.marker.color == d.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"translate s: if d on top/bottom edge → align col(s.marker) to col(d); else → align row(s.marker) to row(d); clip out-of-bounds pixels\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3110\nmechanism=0.3517\nlexical=0.0165\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:closed_region, object:frame, object:grid_edge, object:marker, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/8b7bacbf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8b7bacbf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Find single pixels on grid edges that are endpoints of lines, trace along the line to find connected closed regions, and fill those regions with the edge pixel's color.\",\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"single colored pixels s on grid edge that are endpoints of a line\",\n  \"dst\": \"closed regions d connected to the line\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d is reachable by following the line from s\",\n  \"path\": \"trace along the continuous line from edge pixel s\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"fill interior of each closed region d encountered along path with s.color\",\n  \"transform\": \"d.interior.color = s.color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": null,\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: identify single pixels on grid edge; Step 2: trace the line connected to each edge pixel; Step 3: for each closed region touching the line, flood-fill its interior with edge pixel color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"path-tracing\",\n    \"edge-detection\",\n    \"region-filling\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"98c475bf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2731\nmechanism=0.3753\nlexical=0.0147\ncode_feature=0.1250\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:frame, object:marker, object:sprite, object:template, operation:count, output:same_size, relation:aligned, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/98c475bf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/98c475bf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nErase the complete interior glyph and expand each endpoint marker pair into its color's full glyph.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is 20x20 with background inside two same-color full-height vertical frame bars.\n- Inside the frame there is one complete color glyph and one or more other colors appearing only as two endpoint markers in the same row.\n- Marker endpoints are always in the first and last interior columns.\n\nRule\n- Keep the vertical frame unchanged.\n- Erase any complete interior glyph.\n- For each endpoint marker pair, use that marker color's learned glyph template and anchor its horizontal bar on the marker row.\n\nKey insight\n- Color identifies which glyph shape to draw; the two endpoint pixels are not copied objects, they are anchors for reconstructing that color's full symbol.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"vertical frame containing one complete color glyph and one or more same-row two-pixel endpoint markers of other colors\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase the complete glyph; expand each endpoint marker pair into that marker color's learned glyph template anchored on the marker row\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
